│ Depressive illness is common in old age. Prevalence in the community of case level depression is around 15% and      │
│ milder forms of depression are more common. It causes significant distress and disability. The number of people over │
│ the age of 60 years is expected to double by 2050 and so interventions for this often long‐term and recurrent        │
│ condition are increasingly important. The causes of late‐life depression differ from depression in younger adults    │
│ and so it is appropriate to study it separately.  This is an update of a Cochrane review first published in 2012.    │
│                                                                                                                      │
│ Review objective:                                                                                                    │
│ To examine the efficacy of antidepressants and psychological therapies in preventing the relapse and recurrence of   │
│ depression in older people.                                                                                          │
